  "category": "From GitHub",
  "description": "**From GitHub Issue #559**\n\n## Summary\n\nResearch feasibility of adding Node.js/NAPI bindings to Fluxion for improved adoption in the building energy modeling (BEM) community.\n\n## Motivation\n\nFluxion currently has Python bindings via PyO3/maturin. However, the BEM community uses multiple ecosystems:\n\n- **Node.js/NAPI**: Large portion of BIM tools (Autodesk, Speckle, Trimble) use JavaScript/TypeScript for parametric analysis workflows\n- EnergyPlus OpenStudio SDK is Ruby/JavaScript-based\n- NAPI-RS produces native addons with ~2x faster inference than Python for ONNX workloads\n- Fluxion's 800+ configs/sec throughput would be transformative for JSON-based parametric studies\n\n## Proposed Scope\n\n- [ ] Evaluate `napi-rs` framework vs raw NAPI approach\n- [ ] DesignFFI-friendly API surface for Node.js consumption\n- [ ] Benchmark performance vs Python bindings\n- [ ] Create prototype binding for `BatchOracle::evaluate_population`\n- [ ] Investigate TypeScript type generation\n- [ ] Evaluate cross-compilation for macOS (x64 + ARM), Linux, Windows\n\n## References\n\n- https://napi.rs/ - NAPI-RS framework\n- EnergyPlus/OpenStudio SDK uses JavaScript for parametric workflows\n- Similar projects: ONNX Runtime Node.js bindings, RUFFLE wasm+napi\n\n## Labels\n\n- enhancement\n- research\n- bindings",
